by nicolas-grekas at 2026-07-26T13:40:25Z

**Superseded by the retarget below. The behaviour note still holds; the rest described the earlier 8.2 shape.**

There is one, and it is narrow enough to be worth writing down rather than blocking on.

In a long-running console runner, `Application::reset()` between two commands used to clear the command data. It no longer does, so a record logged after a reset and before the next `ConsoleEvents::COMMAND` now carries the previous command's name instead of none. I probed it with two successive commands on one process:

```
before: cmd:a / <none>  / cmd:b / cmd:b
after:  cmd:a / cmd:a   / cmd:b / cmd:b
```

Records inside a later command stay correct, because `addCommandData` overwrites at `ConsoleEvents::COMMAND` with priority 1, before the command body runs. So there is no cross-contamination between two commands' own logs.

