by nicolas-grekas at 2026-07-26T13:46:55Z

Retargeted from 8.2 to 6.4 and rewritten as an empty `reset()` body instead of removing the interfaces.

The bug is on every maintained branch, and the removal could not be backported, so the fix was landing on the dev branch only. Emptying the body fixes the same thing and is BC safe: nothing public disappears, so an application that hand-tagged the service `kernel.reset` with `method: reset` keeps working. Untagging the service instead is not an option, since the tag is autoconfigured from `ResetInterface`.

The part that decides it is the merge-up. On 7.3 and later the class also implements `Monolog\ResettableInterface`, and `Logger::reset()` cascades into the same `reset()` method, so an empty body neutralizes both paths at once. Checked on 8.2 with the interfaces kept and a test driving the real Monolog cascade: 91 tests green. `git merge-tree` against 7.4, 8.1 and 8.2 is conflict free.

Local runs: 6.4 Monolog bridge 90 tests green, and the new test fails on a clean 6.4 with `Failed asserting that an array has the key 'command'`.

Removing `ResetInterface`, `Monolog\ResettableInterface` and the empty method is still worth doing on 8.2, but as a cleanup on top of this, not as the fix.
